    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nSLAS (Shopper Login and API Access Service) is the authentication backbone for the PWA Kit storefront. Two critical platform-level breaking changes were enforced in production in 2025 — these must be verified before go-live. SLAS clients must be configured separately per site and per environment — cross-environment credential reuse is a common and serious error.\n\n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [SLAS Configuration Guide](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/guide/slas.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [SLAS Admin UI](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/guide/slas-admin-ui.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [Passwordless Login via SLAS](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/guide/slas-passwordless-login.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Release Notes:** [channel\\_id enforcement — Sept 2025](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/about-commerce-api/about.html)\n\n**⚠️ Critical platform change (enforced 9 Sept 2025):** The `channel_id` (site) parameter is now **required** when requesting a guest access token with `grant_type` of `client_credentials` or `authorization_code_pkce`. Missing this parameter causes a `400 invalid refresh token` error and breaks guest browsing entirely.\n\n**⚠️ Platform change (v25.3):** Hybrid Auth replaces Plugin SLAS. If the implementation used Plugin SLAS, it must be migrated.\n\n---\n\nChecklist\n---------\n\n### SLAS Client Configuration\n\n1\n20f0e9923749\ncomplete\nSLAS private client configured for the PWA Kit per environment\n\n2\n010cc8386c8b\nincomplete\n~~SLAS client IDs are unique per site (AU, UK, US Domestic, US Intl, EU Domestic, EU Intl, ME)~~\n\n3\n29316fa2a8fa\ncomplete\nSLAS clients are **not shared** across production and non-production environments\n\n4\nfff29bd1b3ee\nincomplete\nRedirect URIs registered for all production storefront domains\n\n5\ne858e5782306\ncomplete\nRedirect URIs registered for all staging URLs\n\n6\n2f68c58715ce\ncomplete\nRedirect URIs registered for all UAT URLs\n\n### Critical: channel\\_id Parameter Enforcement\n\n7\ne9594ae62937\nincomplete\n~~channel\\_id parameter is included in all guest access token requests (client\\_credentials grant)~~\n\n8\na7ccd0763e6d\nincomplete\n~~channel\\_id parameter is included in all PKCE auth flows (authorization\\_code\\_pkce grant)~~\n\n9\n40bb9b467b70\nincomplete\nGuest browsing tested end-to-end on all seven storefronts without 400 errors\n\n10\nedeb3d3a3096\nincomplete\nSLAS error logs checked in Log Centre for any 400/authentication failures\n\n### ~~Hybrid Auth (v25.3+)~~\n\n11\n55ae499e3390\nincomplete\n~~Confirm whether implementation used Plugin SLAS or native Hybrid Auth~~\n\n12\naef39f41026d\nincomplete\n~~If Plugin SLAS was used, confirm migration to Hybrid Auth is complete~~\n\n13\n5d5f0f2a1074\nincomplete\n~~Hybrid Auth tested on all storefront guest and registered flows~~\n\n### Authentication Flows — End-to-End Testing\n\n14\n11ae93348f39\nincomplete\nGuest checkout flow working (guest token, basket creation, order submission)\n\n15\ndec01634e810\nincomplete\nRegistered login via email/password working (PKCE flow)\n\n16\nf1003710d177\nincomplete\nPasswordless OTP login working — email template configured in BM\n\n17\nf3d7281eca67\nincomplete\nSocial login (Google) working — redirect URIs registered with Google OAuth app\n\n18\n90f2f0596089\nincomplete\nSocial login (Apple) working — redirect URIs registered with Apple\n\n19\n18f11cd40ff9\nincomplete\nRegistered login → basket merge working (guest basket merges into registered basket on login)\n\n20\nb6e465ddf6d6\nincomplete\n\"Remember me\" / persistent session working correctly\n\n### SLAS Token Scopes\n\n21\n43f09825e0d1\ncomplete\nSLAS client scopes reviewed — only required scopes granted (principle of least privilege)\n\n22\n52e9282237f5\ncomplete\nNo SLAS client has excessive scopes (e.g. admin scopes on a public client)\n\n---\n\nNotes / Findings\n----------------\n\n*Record gaps, decisions, and owner for remediation here.*\n\n| Finding | Severity | Owner | Resolved |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  |  |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
