    "id": "407666693",
    "title": "TSD: VIC Exclusive Product Visibility",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/407666693",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Document Information\n--------------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-SFCC-303 |\n| **Author(s)** | Victor T. Crisostomo — Technical Architect / Squad A |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | [Lead name] — Technical Lead |\n| **Created** | 12 Aug 2026 |\n| **Version** | v0.1 — Draft |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Related Jira** | SFCC-303 |\n\n---\n\nVersion History\n---------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | 12 Aug 2026 | Initial draft | Victor T. Crisostomo |\n\n---\n\n1. Problem Statement\n--------------------\n\n### 1.1 Context\n\nThe Zimmermann storefront serves a VIC (Very Important Customer) segment that has access to exclusive products not available to general customers. Currently, SFCC has no native mechanism to restrict product visibility at the customer group level — all products are visible to all users regardless of segment.\n\n### 1.2 Problem\n\nSite Merchandisers have no way to flag a product as VIC-exclusive in Business Manager. Without this, VIC-exclusive products are either exposed to all customers (a brand and commercial risk) or must be withheld from the catalogue entirely (a merchandising limitation). There is no per-product visibility gate tied to customer group membership.\n\n### 1.3 Impact if Not Solved\n\nVIC-exclusive products cannot be listed on the storefront without being visible to all customers, undermining the exclusivity proposition for the VIC segment and potentially damaging the brand relationship with VIC customers.\n\n### 1.4 Success Criteria\n\n* A VIC-exclusive product does not appear in search results for non-VIC customers.\n* A VIC-exclusive product does not appear in category browsing for non-VIC customers.\n* A non-VIC customer navigating directly to a VIC-exclusive PDP URL receives a 404 response.\n* A VIC customer can search, browse, and view VIC-exclusive products without restriction.\n* A Site Merchandiser can set the VIC-exclusive flag on a product in Business Manager without developer intervention.\n\n---\n\n2. Constraints & Assumptions\n----------------------------\n\n### 2.1 Constraints\n\n| Constraint | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Platform | SFCC B2C Commerce + SCAPI (headless). No alternative platform is in scope. |\n| No native SFCC customer-group visibility | SFCC does not support product-level visibility tied to customer groups out of the box. Custom implementation required. |\n| Storefront scope | Solution must work across all active storefronts. No single-market workarounds. |\n| No catalog restructuring | Solution must not require separate catalogs or category structures per customer segment. |\n\n### 2.2 Assumptions\n\n| Assumption | Risk if Wrong |\n| --- | --- |\n| VIC customers are identified via a named SFCC customer group (e.g. \"VIC\") assigned at login or via CRM sync. | If VIC status is determined outside SFCC (e.g. CRM attribute not surfaced to session), the session-level group check will not work and an alternative session enrichment mechanism is needed. |\n| The `isVICExclusive` product attribute can be added to the search index via standard re-indexing. | If the attribute is not indexable, the SCAPI search hook cannot filter on it and an alternative runtime lookup would be required — adding latency. |\n| Non-VIC customers should receive a 404 (not a 403 or a redirect) on direct PDP access, to avoid disclosing product existence. | If requirements change to show a \"not available\" message, the controller guard logic changes and SEO implications must be re-assessed. |\n\n---\n\n3. Options Analysis\n-------------------\n\n### 3.1 Options Summary\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Viable? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Option A** — Custom attribute + SCAPI search hook + PDP guard | + Single-storefront, no catalog restructuring + Merchandiser-controlled in BM + Enforced at both search and PDP layers | - Requires re-indexing on attribute change - Hook implementation adds maintenance surface | Yes — Recommended |\n| **Option B** — Separate catalog per customer segment | + Native SFCC mechanism + No custom hook required | - Requires catalog duplication and ongoing sync - Significant merchandising overhead - Violates no-catalog-restructuring constraint | No |\n| **Option C** — Category-level visibility (assign VIC products to hidden category) | + Simple BM configuration | - Cannot gate by customer group natively - Products hidden from all users, not just non-VIC - Does not meet success criteria | No |\n\n### 3.2 Option Detail\n\n#### Option A — Custom attribute + SCAPI search hook + PDP guard (Recommended)\n\nA custom boolean product attribute `isVICExclusive` is added to the product object and made manageable via Business Manager. The attribute is indexed into the SFCC search index. A SCAPI search hook injects a refinement filter at query time to exclude VIC-exclusive products from results for non-VIC sessions. A separate controller-level guard handles direct PDP URL access. This satisfies all constraints — no catalog restructuring, works across all storefronts, and is fully merchandiser-controlled.\n\n#### Option B — Separate catalog per customer segment (Discarded)\n\nDiscarded — requires maintaining duplicate catalog structures per segment, violates the no-catalog-restructuring constraint, and introduces significant ongoing merchandising overhead.\n\n#### Option C — Category-level hidden category (Discarded)\n\nDiscarded — SFCC category visibility is binary (all users or no users) and cannot be gated by customer group. Does not meet the success criteria.\n\n---\n\n4. Recommended Option & Rationale\n---------------------------------\n\n### 4.1 Recommended Option\n\n**Option A — Custom attribute + SCAPI search hook + PDP guard**\n\n### 4.2 Rationale\n\nOption A is the only approach that satisfies all constraints without catalog restructuring and without introducing a dependency on platform capabilities SFCC does not natively offer. It enforces visibility at both the search layer (preventing discovery) and the PDP layer (preventing direct URL access), fully meeting the success criteria. Merchandiser control via Business Manager requires no developer involvement for day-to-day flagging.\n\n### 4.3 Trade-offs Accepted\n\nRe-indexing is required when the `isVICExclusive` attribute is added or changed on a product. For large catalogues, there may be a delay between a Merchandiser setting the flag in BM and the change being reflected in search results. This is accepted as a known SFCC platform behaviour and should be documented in the Merchandiser runbook.\n\n---\n\n5. Technical Implementation\n---------------------------\n\n### 5.1 High-Level Sequence\n\n1. Site Merchandiser sets `isVICExclusive = true` on the product in Business Manager.\n2. Standard SFCC re-indexing propagates the attribute value to the search index.\n3. Customer initiates a product search or browses a category on the storefront.\n4. SCAPI search hook intercepts the search request and evaluates the session customer group.\n5. If the customer is not in the VIC group, the hook injects a refinement filter: `isVICExclusive = false` (or absent). VIC-exclusive products are excluded from results.\n6. If the customer is in the VIC group, no filter is injected. All products including VIC-exclusive ones are returned.\n7. Customer navigates directly to a PDP URL for a VIC-exclusive product.\n8. Controller-level guard checks `isVICExclusive` on the product and the session customer group.\n9. If not VIC-eligible, return HTTP 404. If VIC-eligible, render PDP normally.\n\n### 5.2 Component / API Changes\n\n| File / Endpoint | Change Required | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| BM Product Attribute Definition | Add `isVICExclusive` boolean attribute to the product system object. Mark as searchable/indexable. | New |\n| SCAPI Search Hook (`dw.ocapi.shop.product.search`) | Inject refinement filter on `isVICExclusive` based on session customer group membership. | New |\n| PDP Controller (Product-Show or equivalent) | Add guard: if product `isVICExclusive = true` and customer group ≠ VIC, return 404. | Modified |\n| Search Index Configuration | Add `isVICExclusive` to indexed and refineable product attributes in Search Preferences. | Modified |\n\n### 5.3 Data Structures / Interfaces\n\njsonwide760// Product custom attribute\n{\n\"attributeId\": \"isVICExclusive\",\n\"type\": \"boolean\",\n\"defaultValue\": false,\n\"searchable\": true,\n\"refineable\": true\n}\n// SCAPI search hook — refinement injection (non-VIC session)\n{\n\"refinements\": [\n{\n\"attributeId\": \"isVICExclusive\",\n\"value\": \"false\"\n}\n]\n}\n\n### 5.4 Error Handling & Edge Cases\n\n| Scenario | Expected Behaviour | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Non-VIC customer hits VIC-exclusive PDP URL directly (e.g. via shared link) | HTTP 404 returned. Product existence is not disclosed. | Edge case |\n| VIC-exclusive product appears in Google index before flag is set | PDP guard returns 404 regardless of referral source. Existing crawled URLs will return 404 until de-indexed by search engines. | Edge case |\n| Customer group session data is missing or null | Treat as non-VIC. Apply the exclusion filter. Fail closed, not open. | Error |\n| Re-index not run after `isVICExclusive` flag set in BM | Product remains visible in search until re-index completes. PDP guard still enforces access at page level. No data exposure risk — only a search visibility lag. | Edge case |\n\n### 5.5 Configuration & Environment Notes\n\n* Custom attribute must be created in BM under **Merchant Tools > Products > Attributes** and assigned to the product system object.\n* Attribute must be added to Search Preferences as an indexed and refineable attribute.\n* Re-indexing required after attribute creation and after any bulk update to product flags.\n* VIC customer group must exist in BM under **Merchant Tools > Customers > Customer Groups** with consistent naming used by the hook and controller.\n\n---\n\n6. Testing & Validation\n-----------------------\n\n### 6.1 Test Coverage\n\n| Test Type | What is Being Tested | Pass Criteria |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Unit | SCAPI search hook refinement injection logic | Hook returns `isVICExclusive = false` filter for non-VIC session; no filter injected for VIC session. |\n| Unit | PDP controller guard logic | Returns 404 for non-VIC customer on VIC-exclusive product; renders normally for VIC customer. |\n| Integration | Search results returned via SCAPI for non-VIC session | No products with `isVICExclusive = true` appear in results. |\n| Integration | Search results returned via SCAPI for VIC session | VIC-exclusive products appear in results alongside non-exclusive products. |\n| E2E / Playwright @p0 | Non-VIC customer searches for VIC-exclusive product keyword | Product does not appear in search results or category pages. |\n| E2E / Playwright @p0 | Non-VIC customer navigates directly to VIC-exclusive PDP URL | 404 page is displayed. |\n| E2E / Playwright | VIC customer searches and views VIC-exclusive product | Product appears in search results and PDP renders correctly. |\n\n### 6.2 Regression Risk\n\nThe SCAPI search hook touches the product search pipeline. Risk of regression is medium — any change to the hook has the potential to affect all search results across all storefronts. Mitigation: existing search E2E suite must pass in full before merge. Specific regression checks: general search for non-exclusive products returns expected results for both VIC and non-VIC customers.\n\n---\n\n7. Risks & Mitigations\n----------------------\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| VIC customer group naming is inconsistent across environments (sandbox vs staging vs prod) | Med | Externalise customer group name as a site preference or environment variable. Do not hardcode. | Tech Lead |\n| Re-index lag causes VIC-exclusive products to remain visible in search after flag is set | High | PDP guard enforces access at page level regardless of index state. Document expected lag in Merchandiser runbook. Consider scheduling re-index as part of the flagging workflow. | Merchandiser / Dev |\n| Search hook causes performance degradation on high-traffic search queries | Low | Hook logic is a simple session group check and refinement injection — no external calls. Load test search endpoint with hook enabled before go-live. | Tech Lead |\n| CRM-to-SFCC customer group sync not in place for VIC segment | Med | Confirm VIC customer group assignment mechanism with CRM/integration team before dev starts. Block implementation if not confirmed. | Technical Architect |\n\n---\n\n8. Decision Record\n------------------\n\n| Date | Decision Maker | Decision | Outcome / Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 12 Aug 2026 | Victor T. Crisostomo, Technical Architect | Adopt Option A: custom attribute + SCAPI search hook + PDP controller guard | Only viable option satisfying no-catalog-restructuring constraint and BM merchandiser control requirement. Discussed and agreed during SFCC-303 refinement. |\n| [DD MMM] | [Name, Role] | TSD approved for implementation | Approved — no changes required |\n\n### Sign-off\n\n| Role | Name | Date | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Author | Victor T. Crisostomo | 12 Aug 2026 | Submitted |\n| Technical Lead / Reviewer | [Name] | [DD MMM YYYY] | Approved / Changes Required |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f4cb",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

