  "metadata": {
    "id": "309657601",
    "title": "Business Manager Configuration Management",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/309657601",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 3,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "business-manager-configuration-managementBusiness Manager Configuration Management\n==================================================================================\n\nThis document defines how Business Manager configuration is managed across environments — what lives in source control, what is applied once at sandbox creation, and what is owned directly in BM.\n\n> **Audience:** Architects, Senior Developers, Platform Team\n\n---\n\nprinciplesPrinciples\n--------------------\n\n| Principle | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Source-controlled config** | Structural metadata that must be consistent across all environments lives in `data/` and is imported via `sfcc-ci instance:import` |\n| **Automated first-time config** | Instance-level settings (WebDAV, OCAPI) are applied once at sandbox creation via the `zimmermann-sfcc-admin` GitHub Action — never manually |\n| **BM-owned config** | Operational and merchandising config that varies per environment or changes frequently is managed directly in BM and is not in source control |\n\n---\n\n1-sourcecontrolled--datacore1. Source-Controlled — `data/core/`\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\nImported via `npm run data:import:core`. Re-importable at any time; safe to re-run on an existing sandbox.\n\n| Asset | Path | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Site definitions | `sites/{SiteID}/site.xml` | Currency, taxation, cartridge path |\n| Site preferences | `sites/{SiteID}/preferences.xml` | Catalog, locales, pricebooks, inventory list assignments |\n| Search profiles | `sites/{SiteID}/search2.xml` | Sorting rules, search refinements |\n| Storefront catalogs | `catalogs/zimmermann-*-storefront-catalog/` | Category structure per site |\n| Master catalog | `catalogs/zimmermann-catalog/` | Shared product classification |\n| Pricebooks | `pricebooks/*.xml` | Empty shells — structure only, no prices |\n| Inventory lists | `inventory-lists/*.xml` | Empty shells — structure only, no stock |\n| Shared library | `libraries/ZimmermannSharedLibrary/` | Shared content library |\n| Customer list | `customer-lists/ZimmermannCommon.xml` | Shared customer list |\n| System object extensions | `meta/system-objecttype-extensions.xml` | Custom attributes on standard objects |\n| Custom object definitions | `meta/custom-objecttype-definitions.xml` | Custom object types |\n| Org-level preferences | `preferences.xml` | ActiveLocales |\n\n**Rule:** If a structural change needs to be the same on every sandbox, staging, and production — it belongs here.\n\n---\n\n2-sourcecontrolled--datavendor2. Source-Controlled — `data/vendor/`\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nImported via `npm run data:import:vendor`. Maintained manually — never auto-generated.\n\n| Vendor | What's imported |\n| --- | --- |\n| Global-e | Services, jobs, custom object type definitions, system object extensions, payment methods, shipping methods |\n| Avalara | Services, custom preferences, tax class metadata |\n\n**Rule:** When a vendor package is upgraded, a developer manually copies the relevant metadata into `data/vendor/<vendor>/` and commits it. `vendor:install` only copies cartridges.\n\n---\n\n3-automated-firsttime--zimmermannsfccadmin-github-action3. Automated First-Time — `zimmermann-sfcc-admin` GitHub Action\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nApplied **once** when a sandbox is created via the `Create Sandbox` GitHub Action in the [zimmermann-sfcc-admin](https://github.com/ZimmermannAU/zimmermann-sfcc-admin) repo. Not re-imported after that.\n\n| Setting | Where applied | Managed after creation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| WebDAV client permissions | Passed to `sfcc-ci sandbox:create --webdav-settings` | Directly in BM if changed |\n| OCAPI Data API settings | Passed to `sfcc-ci sandbox:create --ocapi-settings` | Directly in BM if changed |\n| OCAPI Shop API settings | Passed to `sfcc-ci sandbox:create --ocapi-settings` | Directly in BM if changed |\n\nThese configs live in the `zimmermann-sfcc-admin` repo, not in [`zimmermann-sfcc`](https://github.com/ZimmermannAU/zimmermann-sfcc/).\n\n**Rule:** These are instance-level settings that the sandbox API only needs at creation time. If you need to update them on a running sandbox, do it directly in BM → Administration.\n\n---\n\n4-bmowned--not-in-source-control4. BM-Owned — Not in Source Control\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThese are configured directly in Business Manager and are not tracked in this repo. They vary per environment or are owned by non-developers.\n\n### 4a-onetime--firsttime-setup-done-once-per-sandbox-then-bmowned4a. One-time / First-time Setup (done once per sandbox, then BM-owned)\n\n| Configuration | BM Path |\n| --- | --- |\n| Storefront catalog assignment per site | BM → Merchant Tools → Catalog → Manage Catalogs → assign to site |\n| Code version activation | BM → Administration → Code Deployment |\n| Search index rebuild | BM → Merchant Tools → Search → Search Indexes → rebuild |\n| Site map generation | BM → Merchant Tools → SEO → Sitemaps |\n\n### 4b-operational-config-ongoing-bmowned4b. Operational Config (ongoing, BM-owned)\n\n| Configuration | BM Path | Who manages |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Payment processors | BM → Merchant Tools → Ordering → Payment Processors | Platform team |\n| Shipping methods & rates | BM → Merchant Tools → Ordering → Shipping | Merchandising |\n| Tax rates & tables | BM → Merchant Tools → Ordering → Taxation | Finance / Platform |\n| Promotions & coupons | BM → Merchant Tools → Marketing | Merchandising |\n| Email templates | BM → Merchant Tools → Content → Email | Marketing |\n| A/B test configs | BM → Merchant Tools → Online Marketing | Merchandising |\n| Job schedules | BM → Administration → Operations → Jobs | Platform team |\n| Log levels | BM → Administration → Operations → Log Center | Platform team |\n\n### 4c-credentials--secrets-never-in-source-control4c. Credentials & Secrets (never in source control)\n\n| Configuration | Where it lives |\n| --- | --- |\n| Payment gateway credentials | BM → Site Preferences → Custom Preferences |\n| Global-e merchant token | BM → Site Preferences → Custom Preferences → GlobalE\\_\\* |\n| Avalara account credentials | BM → Site Preferences → Custom Preferences → AvaTax\\_\\* |\n| SFCC AM client secret | GitHub Secrets → `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` (admin repo only) |\n| Developer access keys | `dw.json` — gitignored, local only |\n\n---\n\ndecision-guideDecision Guide\n----------------------------\n\nWhen you need to make a BM configuration change, use this to decide where it goes:\n\nnoneIs it structural metadata that every environment must have?\n└── YES → data/core/ (PR + data:import:core)\n└── NO → Is it vendor integration metadata?\n└── YES → data/vendor/ (PR + data:import:vendor)\n└── NO → Is it an instance-level API permission for a new sandbox?\n└── YES → zimmermann-sfcc-admin repo (sandbox creation action)\n└── NO → Manage directly in BM\n\n---\n\npromoting-config-from-sandbox-to-productionPromoting Config from Sandbox to Production\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n`data/core/` and `data/vendor/` are the promotion path for structural config — import on sandbox, test, merge to main, then import on staging and production via the same `sfcc-ci instance:import` commands.\n\nBM-owned config (section 4b) is promoted manually using BM → Site Import & Export or replicated directly in each environment by the responsible team.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "2699-fe0f",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

